<Item XName="Readme" UserName="Readme" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;256-APSK for DVB-S2X evaluation&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue&amp;nbsp;Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;1. This workspace sets up a custom 256-APSK signal source according to specifications in the&amp;nbsp;DVB-S2X physical layer document, dated March 2014.&amp;nbsp; The signal is then demodulated it using he 89600 VSA (with Option AYA, for vector demod).&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;2. This is an uncoded signal, no framing, no DSSS applied.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The &lt;EM&gt;DigitalMod&lt;/EM&gt; part is&amp;nbsp;configured to generate the custom APSK format.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; The ring ratios are nonlinear and provide a small amount of pre-distortion for AM/AM effects in the PA.&amp;nbsp; The 89600 VSA .setx file mirrors these ring ratios so that you can look directly at EVM.&amp;nbsp; The slider allows you to change the amplitude into the PA and see the EVM change.&amp;nbsp; Two different PA models are offered, one is a TWTA as referenced in the standard, the other is a regular compressing amplifier model.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;EVM is also partly affected by the phase noise on the LO.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;FONT size=2&gt; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;3. This basic &lt;EM&gt;DigitalMod&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;signal source is included free with the core SystemVue environment.&amp;nbsp; For more complete demodulation, reference receiver, and EVM/BER &amp;nbsp;directly in SystemVue, you can use the W1902 Digital Modem library.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
